From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a website frame runs its scriptlets at document
 start

A site's `##+js(...)` rules name scriptlets that must run before the
page's own scripts. Blink forbids script while it tells a
RenderFrameObserver the document's element exists
(FrameLoader::DispatchDocumentElementAvailable), so
domicile::CosmeticFilters cannot run them there. Script may run just
after, in ContentRendererClient::RunScriptsAtDocumentStart, where
extensions' `document_start` scripts run: ChromeContentRendererClient
now runs the frame's scriptlets there, after an Electron app window's
preload and before extensions', and starts its procedural filters in an
isolated world of their own, ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS.
See components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. Guarded by guard-ad-blocking.
---
 chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h         | 4 ++++
 chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h b/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
index d158c41755..09816fe93d 100644
--- a/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
+++ b/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@ enum ChromeIsolatedWorldIDs {
   ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_APPLESCRIPT,
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the ad blocker's procedural filters. See
+  // components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.
+  ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS,
+
   // Numbers for isolated worlds for extensions are set in
   // extensions/renderer/script_injection.cc, and are are greater than or equal
   // to this number.

diff --git a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
index f288108..4e91b9e 100644
--- a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
@@ -1596,6 +1596,15 @@ void ChromeContentRendererClient::RunScriptsAtDocumentStart(
     return;
   }
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork. The scriptlets a website's filter rules name,
+  // before the page's scripts and extensions', and its procedural filters,
+  // in a world of their own. The scriptlets are page scripts and may end the
+  // frame. See components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.
+  if (!domicile::CosmeticFilters::RunAtDocumentStart(
+          render_frame, ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS)) {
+    return;
+  }
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_EXTENSIONS_CORE)
   extensions::ExtensionsRendererClient::Get()->RunScriptsAtDocumentStart(
       render_frame);
-- 
